<title>ECUADOR: Ecuador bank liquidity up 3.54 pct in March.</title>
<headline>Ecuador bank liquidity up 3.54 pct in March.</headline>
<dateline>QUITO 1997-04-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Ecuador's Central Bank said Tuesday liquidity in the banking system grew 3.54 percent or 651 million sucres to 19.03 billion sucres in March.</p>
<p>At the end of February, bank liquidity stood at 18.38 billion sucres.</p>
<p>Total liquidity in the banking sector ended 1996 at 16.99 billion sucres, up 35.8 percent from 1995.</p>
<p>((--Gustavo Oviedo, Quito Newsroom, +5932 258429, e-mail: reuters1@reutersecu.com.ec))</p>
